# dconf key locks -- values set in ../01-peachos that a user (or an extension's
# own prefs UI, or a schema-version migration) must not be able to override.
#
# blur-my-shell panel blur: macos-top-panel owns the menu bar look. Without
# these locks, blur-my-shell kept repainting a blurred/!opaque top bar on
# fresh installs regardless of the peachOS Menu Bar switch (that switch drives
# macos-top-panel's own menu-bar-blur key, a different mechanism entirely).
/org/gnome/shell/extensions/blur-my-shell/panel/blur
/org/gnome/shell/extensions/blur-my-shell/panel/override-background
